{"uid":"src/flex_layout.c::fx_auto_min_size","name":"fx_auto_min_size","qualname":"fx_auto_min_size","kind":"function","file":"src/flex_layout.c","line":636,"end_line":651,"language":"c","signature":"double fx_auto_min_size(double min_content, double basis, double author_min, int scroll_container)","params":[{"name":"min_content","annotation":"double","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"basis","annotation":"double","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"author_min","annotation":"double","default":"","kind":"positional"},{"name":"scroll_container","annotation":"int","default":"","kind":"positional"}],"returns":"double","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"Automatic minimum size of a flex item along the main axis (CSS Flexbox 4.5), in px.","description":"This is what `min-width: auto` -- the INITIAL value, so the case for almost every item on the web -- resolves to. It is the floor fx_flex_line must not shrink an item below, and getting it wrong is visible everywhere: with a floor of zero an overflowing line grinds every item down to a sliver and its text falls to one character per line.\n\nmin_content  the item's min-content size (its longest unbreakable word, or a\n               replaced element's intrinsic size), in the same border-box+margin\n               units as fx_item.basis. Negative is treated as 0.\n  basis        the item's SPECIFIED size (its declared `width`, in the same units),\n               the \"specified size suggestion\": the content-based minimum is clamped\n               by it, so an item the author sized small is not inflated by one long\n               word. Negative means no specified size and leaves the minimum at\n               min-content; a flex-basis is NOT a specified size.\n  author_min   the author's own `min-width` in px when they set one (min-width is\n               then NOT `auto` and wins outright, larger OR smaller), or < 0 when\n               unset.\n  scroll_container  non-zero when the item's `overflow` is anything but `visible`.\n               Such an item has an automatic minimum size of ZERO -- this is what\n               makes the near-universal `overflow:hidden` truncation idiom work.\n\nPure, total, no allocation. The result is never negative.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[["Inherited","Documentation from `fx_auto_min_size` (include/flex_layout.h:275)."]],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"src/flex_layout.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
